<!DOCTYPE html>
<html lang="en">
<head>
<meta charset="UTF-8">
<meta name="viewport" content="width=device-width, initial-scale=1.0">
<title>Deaths by Suicide — Crown Dependencies &amp; England/Wales · Crown Dependencies Re-Identification Observatory</title>
<link rel="preconnect" href="https://fonts.googleapis.com"/>
<link href="https://fonts.googleapis.com/css2?family=Inter:wght@300;400;500;600;700;800&family=JetBrains+Mono:wght@400;600&display=swap" rel="stylesheet"/>
<script async src="https://plausible.io/js/pa-BgIsm1huogpQ9ffMmmnIF.js">

/* ── OBSERVATORY THEME SYNC ──────────────────────────────────────────────────
   Receives light/dark instructions from the parent App shell.
────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────── */
(function () {
  if (window.__obsThemeReady) return;
  window.__obsThemeReady = true;
  function applyTheme(isLight) {
    document.body.classList.toggle('light', isLight);
  }
  window.addEventListener('message', function (e) {
    if (e.data && e.data.type === 'observatory-theme') {
      applyTheme(!!e.data.light);
    }
  });
  // Ask parent for current theme as soon as possible
  if (window.parent !== window) {
    window.parent.postMessage({ type: 'observatory-theme-request' }, '*');
  }
}());
</script>
<script>
  window.plausible=window.plausible||function(){(plausible.q=plausible.q||[]).push(arguments)},plausible.init=plausible.init||function(i){plausible.o=i||{}};
  plausible.init()
</script>
<style>
  *, *::before, *::after { box-sizing: border-box; margin: 0; padding: 0; }
  :root {
    --bg:#0f172a; --surface:#1e293b; --surface2:#162032;
    --border:#1e293b; --border2:#334155;
    --text:#e2e8f0; --muted:#94a3b8; --muted2:#64748b;
    --blue:#60a5fa; --blue-dim:#1d4ed8; --green:#34d399;
    --amber:#fbbf24; --red:#f87171; --purple:#a78bfa; --orange:#fb923c;
    --iom:#3b82f6; --gsy:#10b981; --jsy:#f59e0b;
    /* chart aliases */
    --c-ew:var(--blue); --c-iom:var(--red); --c-gy:var(--gsy); --c-jsy:var(--jsy);
    /* canvas helpers */
    --cvs:#0f172a; --grid:#1e293b; --tick:#64748b;
    /* age band palette — purple ramp within --purple token */
    --age0:#c4b5fd; --age1:#a78bfa; --age2:#7c3aed; --age3:#94a3b8; --age4:#475569;
  }
  html, body {
    font-family: 'Inter', system-ui, sans-serif;
    background: var(--bg); color: var(--text);
    font-size: 14px; line-height: 1.5;
    -webkit-font-smoothing: antialiased;
  }
  .shell { max-width: 960px; margin: 0 auto; padding: 20px 20px 40px; }

  /* Page header */
  .eyebrow { font-size:10px; font-weight:700; color:var(--muted2); text-transform:uppercase;
    letter-spacing:0.10em; margin-bottom:4px; }
  h1 { font-size:20px; font-weight:800; letter-spacing:-0.02em; color:var(--text); margin-bottom:4px; }
  .subtitle { font-size:12px; color:var(--muted); margin-bottom:16px; }

  /* Support banner — Samaritans guideline */
  .support-banner {
    background:rgba(96,165,250,0.07); border:1px solid rgba(96,165,250,0.25);
    border-left:3px solid var(--blue); border-radius:8px; padding:10px 14px;
    margin-bottom:16px; font-size:12px; color:var(--muted); line-height:1.7;
  }
  .support-banner strong { color:var(--text); }
  .support-banner a { color:var(--blue); text-decoration:none; }

  .warn { background:rgba(251,191,36,0.08); border:1px solid rgba(251,191,36,0.3);
    border-left:3px solid var(--amber); border-radius:8px; padding:10px 14px; margin-bottom:16px;
    font-size:12px; color:var(--amber); font-weight:500; }
  .card { background:var(--surface); border:1px solid var(--border2); border-radius:10px;
    overflow:visible; margin-bottom:14px; }

  /* View tabs — brief-compliant colours */
  .view-tabs { display:flex; gap:4px; padding:10px 12px; border-bottom:1px solid var(--border2);
    background:var(--surface2); border-radius:10px 10px 0 0; flex-wrap:wrap; align-items:center; }
  .view-tab { border:none; border-bottom:2px solid transparent; padding:6px 14px;
    font-size:12px; font-weight:500; font-family:'Inter',sans-serif; cursor:pointer;
    background:transparent; color:#94a3b8; transition:color 0.15s; margin-bottom:-1px; }
  .view-tab.active { color:#93c5fd; font-weight:600; border-bottom-color:#93c5fd; }
  .view-tab:hover:not(.active) { color:#cbd5e1; }
  .view-tab.iom-tab { color:var(--red); border-color:transparent; margin-left:12px; }
  .view-tab.iom-tab.active { color:#93c5fd; border-bottom-color:#93c5fd; }
  #tab-unemp { color:var(--blue); }

  /* Series toggles */
  .toggles { display:flex; flex-wrap:wrap; gap:6px; padding:8px 12px;
    border-bottom:1px solid var(--border2); align-items:center; }
  .toggle-btn { border:2px solid transparent; border-radius:20px; padding:3px 12px;
    font-size:11px; font-family:'JetBrains Mono',monospace; font-weight:600;
    cursor:pointer; background:transparent; transition:all 0.18s; white-space:nowrap; }

  #chart-wrap { position:relative; width:100%; max-width:900px; }
  canvas { display:block; width:100%; height:auto; }

  #tooltip { position:absolute; pointer-events:none; background:var(--surface);
    border:1px solid var(--border2); border-radius:8px; padding:10px 13px; font-size:12px;
    box-shadow:0 4px 20px rgba(0,0,0,0.35); min-width:180px; max-width:280px; display:none; z-index:10; }
  .t-year { font-weight:700; font-size:13px; margin-bottom:6px; color:var(--text); }
  .t-row { margin-bottom:4px; display:flex; align-items:flex-start; gap:6px; }
  .t-dot { width:10px; height:10px; border-radius:50%; flex-shrink:0; margin-top:2px; }
  .t-val { font-weight:600; color:var(--text); }
  .t-note { color:var(--muted2); font-size:11px; }

  .legend-bar { display:flex; flex-wrap:wrap; gap:6px 18px; padding:8px 14px;
    border-top:1px solid var(--border2); font-size:11px; color:var(--muted);
    background:var(--surface2); border-radius:0 0 10px 10px; }
  .leg { display:flex; align-items:center; gap:5px; }

  /* Notes section */
  .notes-hdr { padding:12px 16px; display:flex; justify-content:space-between; align-items:center;
    cursor:pointer; user-select:none; border-bottom:1px solid var(--border2);
    background:var(--surface2); border-radius:10px 10px 0 0; }
  .notes-hdr h2 { font-size:13px; font-weight:700; color:var(--text); }
  .notes-hdr .hint { font-size:11px; color:var(--muted); }
  .notes-body { padding:0 16px 16px; background:var(--surface); border-radius:0 0 10px 10px; }
  .nb { margin-top:14px; }
  .nb h3 { font-size:11px; font-weight:700; margin-bottom:6px; display:flex; align-items:center; gap:8px;
    color:var(--muted); text-transform:uppercase; letter-spacing:0.06em; }
  .jdot { width:10px; height:10px; border-radius:50%; flex-shrink:0; }
  .nb ul { list-style:disc; padding-left:18px; }
  .nb li { font-size:12px; color:var(--muted); line-height:1.65; margin-bottom:3px; }
  .al { color:var(--red); font-weight:600; }
  .ok { color:var(--green); font-weight:600; }
  .sources { margin-top:14px; font-size:11px; color:var(--muted2); border-top:1px solid var(--border2); padding-top:10px; }
  .sources p { margin-bottom:3px; }

  /* IoM detail panel */
  .iom-grid { display:grid; grid-template-columns:1fr 1fr; gap:14px; margin-bottom:14px; }
  .iom-subcard { background:var(--surface2); border:1px solid var(--border2); border-radius:8px; padding:10px 12px; }
  .iom-subcard-title { font-size:10px; font-weight:700; color:var(--muted2);
    font-family:'JetBrains Mono',monospace; text-transform:uppercase;
    letter-spacing:0.07em; margin-bottom:8px; }
  .iom-canvas-wrap { position:relative; width:100%; }
  .stat-row { display:grid; grid-template-columns:repeat(3,1fr); gap:10px; margin-bottom:14px; }
  .stat-box { background:var(--surface2); border:1px solid var(--border2); border-radius:8px;
    padding:12px 14px; text-align:center; }
  .stat-val { font-size:22px; font-weight:700; color:var(--text); }
  .stat-val.red { color:var(--red); }
  .stat-val.amber { color:var(--amber); }
  .stat-lbl { font-size:10px; font-weight:700; text-transform:uppercase; letter-spacing:0.07em;
    color:var(--muted2); margin-bottom:4px; }
  .stat-sub { font-size:10px; color:var(--muted2); margin-top:3px; }
  .iom-legend { display:flex; flex-wrap:wrap; gap:8px 18px; font-size:11px;
    color:var(--muted); margin-top:6px; }
  .iom-swatch { display:inline-block; width:10px; height:10px; border-radius:2px;
    vertical-align:middle; margin-right:3px; }

  /* Unemployment overlay panel */
  .unemp-grid { display:grid; grid-template-columns:1fr 1fr; gap:14px; margin-bottom:14px; }
  .unemp-panel-hdr { display:flex; align-items:baseline; gap:10px; flex-wrap:wrap; margin-bottom:6px; }
  .unemp-jur { font-size:11px; font-weight:700; text-transform:uppercase; letter-spacing:.07em;
    font-family:'JetBrains Mono',monospace; }
  .unemp-range { display:flex; gap:3px; margin-left:auto; align-items:center; }
  .unemp-range-lbl { font-size:9px; color:var(--muted2); font-family:'JetBrains Mono',monospace; margin-right:2px; }
  .urbtn { border:1px solid var(--border2); background:transparent; color:var(--muted2);
    font-size:9px; font-family:'JetBrains Mono',monospace; padding:2px 8px; border-radius:3px;
    cursor:pointer; transition:all .15s; }
  .urbtn.active { background:rgba(96,165,250,.12); border-color:var(--blue); color:var(--blue); }
  .urbtn:hover:not(.active) { color:var(--muted); border-color:var(--border2); }
  .unemp-leg { display:flex; flex-wrap:wrap; gap:3px 12px; margin-top:5px;
    font-size:10px; color:var(--muted2); }
  .unemp-leg span { display:flex; align-items:center; gap:4px; }
  .ul-line { display:inline-block; width:14px; height:2px; border-radius:1px; vertical-align:middle; }
  .ul-dot  { display:inline-block; width:8px; height:8px; border-radius:50%; vertical-align:middle; border:1.5px solid #0f172a; }
  .ul-dash { display:inline-block; width:14px; height:0; vertical-align:middle; border-top:2px dashed rgba(251,191,36,0.7); }
  .unemp-note { font-size:10px; color:var(--muted2); margin-top:6px; line-height:1.65; }
  .unemp-note .al { color:var(--amber); font-weight:600; }
  .unemp-note .ok { color:var(--green); font-weight:600; }
  .unemp-narrative { background:rgba(96,165,250,0.04); border:1px solid rgba(96,165,250,0.15);
    border-left:3px solid var(--blue); border-radius:6px; padding:10px 14px;
    margin-bottom:10px; font-size:11px; color:var(--muted); line-height:1.75; }
  .unemp-narrative strong { color:var(--text); }
  .unemp-gov-hdr { padding:8px 12px; background:var(--surface2); border:1px solid var(--border2);
    border-radius:6px; display:flex; justify-content:space-between; align-items:center;
    cursor:pointer; user-select:none; margin-bottom:0; }
  .unemp-gov-hdr h3 { font-size:11px; font-weight:700; color:var(--text); }
  .unemp-gov-hdr .hint { font-size:10px; color:var(--muted2); }
  .unemp-gov-body { display:none; padding:10px 12px 0; }
  .unemp-gov-body.open { display:block; }
  .unemp-gov-body ul { list-style:disc; padding-left:15px; }
  .unemp-gov-body li { font-size:11px; color:var(--muted); line-height:1.65; margin-bottom:2px; }
  .unemp-gov-body .ok { color:var(--green); font-weight:600; }
  .unemp-gov-body .al { color:var(--amber); font-weight:600; }

  /* Support footer */
  .support-footer {
    margin-top:20px; background:var(--surface2); border:1px solid var(--border2);
    border-radius:8px; padding:12px 16px; font-size:12px; color:var(--muted); line-height:1.7;
  }
  .support-footer strong { color:var(--text); }
  .support-footer a { color:var(--blue); text-decoration:none; }

  /* Observatory page footer */
  .page-footer {
    margin-top:32px; padding-top:16px; border-top:1px solid var(--border2);
    font-size:10px; color:var(--muted2);
    display:flex; justify-content:space-between; flex-wrap:wrap; gap:8px;
  }
  .page-footer a { color:var(--muted); text-decoration:none; }
  .page-footer a:hover { color:var(--text); }
body.light {
  --bg: #f8fafc; --surface: #ffffff; --surface2: #f1f5f9;
  --border: #e2e8f0; --border2: #cbd5e1;
  --text: #0f172a; --muted: #64748b; --muted2: #475569;
  --blue: #2563eb; --blue-dim: rgba(37,99,235,0.08);
  --iom: #2563eb; --gsy: #059669; --jsy: #d97706; --uk: #64748b;
  --green: #059669; --amber: #d97706; --red: #dc2626;
  /* canvas helpers for light mode */
  --cvs: #f8fafc; --grid: #e2e8f0; --tick: #64748b;
  --c-ew: #2563eb; --c-iom: #dc2626; --c-gy: #059669; --c-jsy: #d97706;
}
</style>
</head>
<body>
<div class="shell">

<h1>Deaths by Suicide — Crown Dependencies &amp; England/Wales</h1>
<p class="subtitle">Isle of Man · Guernsey · Jersey · England &amp; Wales &nbsp;|&nbsp; Annual counts, crude rates, and age-standardised rates &nbsp;|&nbsp; <em>Updated June 2026</em></p>

<!-- SAMARITANS GUIDELINE: prominent support signposting at top -->
<div class="support-banner">
  <strong>If you or someone you know needs support:</strong> Samaritans are available 24/7, free of charge — call <strong>116 123</strong> or visit <a href="https://www.samaritans.org" target="_blank" rel="noopener">samaritans.org</a>. In the Isle of Man, Lifeline is available on <strong>0808 808 8000</strong>. These statistics describe population-level trends and are intended for public health and policy audiences.
</div>

<div class="warn">
  ⚠ Data sources, methodologies, populations and recording standards differ significantly between jurisdictions. Cross-jurisdictional comparisons require care. See Data Governance Notes below.
</div>

<div class="card" id="main-card">
  <!-- VIEW TABS — outside chart body so they persist on IoM/demog panel -->
  <div id="main-tabs">
    <div class="view-tabs" style="border-radius:10px 10px 0 0; border-bottom:1px solid var(--border2);">
      <span style="font-size:10px;color:var(--muted2);font-family:'JetBrains Mono',monospace;margin-right:4px;">View:</span>
      <button class="view-tab" id="tab-counts">Annual counts</button>
      <button class="view-tab" id="tab-crude">Crude rate /100k</button>
      <button class="view-tab active" id="tab-asmr">3yr rolling ASMR /100k</button>
      <button class="view-tab iom-tab" id="tab-iom">Demographics ↗</button>
      <button class="view-tab iom-tab" id="tab-unemp">Labour market ↗</button>
    </div>
    <div class="view-tabs" id="range-row" style="border-radius:0; border-bottom:1px solid var(--border2); padding:6px 12px;">
      <span style="font-size:10px;color:var(--muted2);font-family:'JetBrains Mono',monospace;margin-right:4px;">Range:</span>
      <button class="view-tab" id="range-all">All years</button>
      <button class="view-tab active" id="range-2006">From 2006</button>
    </div>
  </div>

  <!-- CHART BODY — this is what gets hidden when demographics tab is shown -->
  <div id="chart-body">

  <!-- SERIES TOGGLES -->
  <div class="toggles" id="toggles">
    <button class="toggle-btn" id="btn-ew"  style="border-color:#60a5fa;background:#60a5fa;color:#0f172a;">England &amp; Wales</button>
    <button class="toggle-btn" id="btn-iom" style="border-color:#f87171;background:#f87171;color:#0f172a;">Isle of Man</button>
    <button class="toggle-btn" id="btn-gy"  style="border-color:#34d399;background:#34d399;color:#0f172a;">Guernsey</button>
    <button class="toggle-btn" id="btn-jsy" style="border-color:#a78bfa;background:#a78bfa;color:#0f172a;">Jersey</button>
  </div>

  <div id="chart-wrap">
    <canvas id="chart" width="900" height="440"></canvas>
    <div id="tooltip">
      <div class="t-year" id="t-year"></div>
      <div id="t-rows"></div>
    </div>
  </div>

  <div class="legend-bar" id="legend-bar">
    <!-- filled by JS -->
  </div>

  </div><!-- /chart-body -->
</div><!-- /main-card -->

<!-- DEMOGRAPHICS PANEL -->
<div id="iom-panel" style="display:none;">

  <div style="padding:10px 0 12px;">
    <span style="font-size:10px;font-weight:700;text-transform:uppercase;letter-spacing:0.08em;color:var(--muted2);font-family:'JetBrains Mono',monospace;">Demographics &amp; labour market · Crown Dependencies · 2019–2023</span>
  </div>

  <!-- STAT CARDS — row 1: male rates; row 2: sex% and working age -->
  <div style="display:grid;grid-template-columns:repeat(4,1fr);gap:10px;margin-bottom:8px;">
    <div class="stat-box">
      <div class="stat-lbl">IoM male rate (2019–23)</div>
      <div class="stat-val">23.8</div>
      <div class="stat-sub">per 100k/yr · year of death</div>
    </div>
    <div class="stat-box">
      <div class="stat-lbl">Jersey male rate (2019–23)</div>
      <div class="stat-val">11.1</div>
      <div class="stat-sub">per 100k/yr · est. sex split</div>
    </div>
    <div class="stat-box">
      <div class="stat-lbl">Guernsey male rate (2019–23)</div>
      <div class="stat-val">19.6</div>
      <div class="stat-sub">per 100k/yr · estimated</div>
    </div>
    <div class="stat-box">
      <div class="stat-lbl">E&amp;W male rate (2019–23)</div>
      <div class="stat-val">13.8</div>
      <div class="stat-sub">per 100k/yr · ONS registration</div>
    </div>
  </div>
  <div style="display:grid;grid-template-columns:repeat(4,1fr);gap:10px;margin-bottom:14px;">
    <div class="stat-box">
      <div class="stat-lbl">IoM — sex &amp; age</div>
      <div class="stat-val" style="font-size:15px;line-height:1.3;">76% male</div>
      <div class="stat-sub">58% aged 30–59 · not cross-tabulated</div>
    </div>
    <div class="stat-box">
      <div class="stat-lbl">Jersey — sex &amp; age</div>
      <div class="stat-val" style="font-size:15px;line-height:1.3;">72% male</div>
      <div class="stat-sub">78% aged 25–64 · not cross-tabulated</div>
    </div>
    <div class="stat-box">
      <div class="stat-lbl">Guernsey — sex &amp; age</div>
      <div class="stat-val" style="font-size:15px;line-height:1.3;color:#f59e0b;">55%</div>
      <div class="stat-sub">male AND aged 20–59 · confirmed cross-tab</div>
    </div>
    <div class="stat-box">
      <div class="stat-lbl">E&amp;W — sex &amp; age</div>
      <div class="stat-val" style="font-size:15px;line-height:1.3;">75% male</div>
      <div class="stat-sub">~65% aged 25–64 · ONS est.</div>
    </div>
  </div>

  <!-- SEX RATES CHART — one grouped chart, all four jurisdictions -->
  <div class="iom-subcard" style="margin-bottom:6px;">
    <div class="iom-subcard-title">Average annual deaths per 100,000 by sex — 2019–23 · all jurisdictions · same scale</div>
    <div class="iom-canvas-wrap" style="height:220px;"><canvas id="sex-rate-chart" width="800" height="220"></canvas></div>
  </div>
  <div style="font-size:10px;color:var(--muted2);margin-bottom:14px;line-height:1.6;">
    <span style="display:inline-block;width:12px;height:12px;background:#f87171;border-radius:2px;vertical-align:middle;margin-right:4px;"></span>Male &nbsp;
    <span style="display:inline-block;width:12px;height:12px;background:rgba(248,113,113,0.35);border:1px solid #f87171;border-radius:2px;vertical-align:middle;margin-right:4px;"></span>Female &nbsp;&nbsp;
    IoM: confirmed counts (Constabulary FOI 3968233), year of death. Jersey: 2019–23 counts confirmed; sex split estimated from 2010–23 FOI aggregate (72% male applied). Guernsey: both counts and sex split estimated from 2005–24 Mortality Trends 2024 data. E&amp;W: ONS registration counts, ~74% male applied. Rates use sex-specific population denominators. Confidence intervals wide for island jurisdictions given small absolute numbers.
  </div>

  <!-- EMPLOYMENT ANOMALY CALLOUT -->
  <div style="background:rgba(96,165,250,0.06);border:1px solid rgba(96,165,250,0.2);border-left:3px solid var(--blue);border-radius:8px;padding:14px 16px;margin-bottom:14px;font-size:12px;color:var(--muted);line-height:1.85;">
    <div style="font-size:11px;font-weight:700;text-transform:uppercase;letter-spacing:0.07em;color:var(--blue);margin-bottom:8px;">The employment anomaly</div>
    The Isle of Man government's own suicide prevention strategy audit (GD2023/0019) examined 65 cases from 2016 to 2021. It found that <strong style="color:var(--text);">33% of those who died were unemployed or unable to work</strong> — against <strong style="color:var(--text);">8% of the general working-age population, as measured in the 2021 Census</strong>. That is a <strong style="color:var(--text);">4.1× overrepresentation</strong>.
    <br><br>
    That 8% baseline is not unemployment in the headline sense. The 2021 Census recorded five reasons for economic inactivity. Two are relevant here:
    <br><br>
    <table style="width:100%;border-collapse:collapse;font-size:11px;margin-bottom:10px;">
      <tr style="border-bottom:1px solid var(--border2);">
        <th style="text-align:left;padding:4px 8px 4px 0;color:var(--muted);font-weight:600;">Category</th>
        <th style="text-align:right;padding:4px 8px;color:var(--muted);font-weight:600;">Count</th>
        <th style="text-align:right;padding:4px 8px;color:var(--muted);font-weight:600;">% of working-age</th>
        <th style="text-align:left;padding:4px 0 4px 8px;color:var(--muted);font-weight:600;">Source</th>
      </tr>
      <tr style="border-bottom:1px solid var(--border2);">
        <td style="padding:4px 8px 4px 0;color:var(--muted);">JSA claimants</td>
        <td style="text-align:right;padding:4px 8px;font-family:'JetBrains Mono',monospace;color:var(--text);">~650</td>
        <td style="text-align:right;padding:4px 8px;font-family:'JetBrains Mono',monospace;color:var(--text);">~1.2%</td>
        <td style="padding:4px 0 4px 8px;color:var(--muted2);">Labour Market Report, 2021 avg</td>
      </tr>
      <tr style="border-bottom:1px solid var(--border2);">
        <td style="padding:4px 8px 4px 0;color:var(--muted);">ILO unemployed, not claiming JSA</td>
        <td style="text-align:right;padding:4px 8px;font-family:'JetBrains Mono',monospace;color:var(--text);">~660</td>
        <td style="text-align:right;padding:4px 8px;font-family:'JetBrains Mono',monospace;color:var(--text);">~1.2%</td>
        <td style="padding:4px 0 4px 8px;color:var(--muted2);">2021 Census Table 3.2 (ILO total ~1,309 minus JSA)</td>
      </tr>
      <tr style="border-bottom:1px solid var(--border2);">
        <td style="padding:4px 8px 4px 0;color:var(--muted);">Unable to work — long-term sick or disabled</td>
        <td style="text-align:right;padding:4px 8px;font-family:'JetBrains Mono',monospace;color:var(--text);">2,631</td>
        <td style="text-align:right;padding:4px 8px;font-family:'JetBrains Mono',monospace;color:var(--text);">~5.0%</td>
        <td style="padding:4px 0 4px 8px;color:var(--muted2);">2021 Census Table 3.3</td>
      </tr>
      <tr style="font-weight:600;">
        <td style="padding:6px 8px 4px 0;color:var(--text);">Total</td>
        <td style="text-align:right;padding:6px 8px 4px;font-family:'JetBrains Mono',monospace;color:var(--text);">~3,940</td>
        <td style="text-align:right;padding:6px 8px 4px;font-family:'JetBrains Mono',monospace;color:var(--text);">~7.5% ≈ 8%</td>
        <td style="padding:6px 0 4px 8px;color:var(--muted2);font-weight:400;"></td>
      </tr>
    </table>
    The JSA claimant rate cited in press releases — around 0.6% of total population — represents roughly <strong style="color:var(--text);">one person in six</strong> of that 8% group. The group 4.1× overrepresented in suicide deaths is roughly <strong style="color:var(--text);">thirteen times larger</strong> than the figure quoted when politicians say the island is at full employment.
    <br><br>
    Despite this overrepresentation, the available data does not show a clear correlation between the IoM's unemployment rate and its suicide rate over time. The measurement challenges are substantial — the JSA headline undercounts true unemployment by a factor of several, the ASMR series is short and noisy, and the two series move in opposite directions during 2017–2019. The relationship, if it exists, cannot be demonstrated from what is currently published.
  </div>

  <!-- COMBINED CHART: deaths + JSA + census ILO -->
  <div class="iom-subcard" style="margin-bottom:10px;">
    <div class="iom-subcard-title">IoM — annual suicide deaths (left) · JSA claimant rate % monthly (right) · census ILO snapshots (right) · 2006–2026</div>
    <div class="iom-canvas-wrap" style="height:240px;"><canvas id="iom-overlay-chart" width="800" height="240"></canvas></div>
    <div style="display:flex;gap:16px;margin-top:6px;font-size:10px;color:var(--muted2);flex-wrap:wrap;">
      <span><span style="display:inline-block;width:18px;height:2px;background:#f87171;vertical-align:middle;margin-right:4px;"></span>Deaths — registration year (left axis)</span>
      <span><span style="display:inline-block;width:18px;height:2px;background:rgba(96,165,250,0.7);vertical-align:middle;margin-right:4px;"></span>JSA claimant rate % — monthly (right axis)</span>
      <span><span style="display:inline-block;width:10px;height:10px;background:rgba(96,165,250,0.9);border-radius:50%;vertical-align:middle;margin-right:4px;"></span>Census ILO unemployed (right axis — census day snapshot)</span>
    </div>
    <div style="font-size:10px;color:var(--muted2);margin-top:5px;line-height:1.6;">
      JSA = monthly claimant count as % of total population (not seasonally adjusted — winter peaks visible). JSA excludes: people whose contribution-based entitlement has run out; people with savings, redundancy pay, or a working partner above the means-test threshold; the previously self-employed (whose NI contributions don't qualify for contribution-based JSA); and anyone who has stopped actively looking. Census ILO markers (●) = ILO-defined unemployed as % of total population on census day: 2011=1.75%, 2016=1.37%, 2021=1.56% — consistently above JSA because census falls in May/June at the seasonal JSA trough. Deaths = annual registration counts, plotted as a continuous line through mid-year (July) values (left axis). No causal relationship is asserted.
    </div>
  </div>

  <div class="warn" style="margin-bottom:14px;">
    ⚠ Pre-2019 IoM demographic breakdown not available from the Constabulary. The suicide audit (GD2023/0019) covers 2016–21 (65 cases): 74% male; peak rate 40–44 in men (~46/100k/yr); 59% of deaths in the 35–59 band. FOI recommended to Public Health IoM / General Registry for pre-2019 annual sex/age data.
  </div>

